<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>The Battle of Langkawi, 1973</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;This scenario assumes that&amp;nbsp;a communist insurgency that erupted in Malaysia in the 1970s and 1980s was far more successful than it was in history.&amp;nbsp; By 1973, the communists are assumed to have taken control of most of the Malaysian state of Kedah.&amp;nbsp; They have captured a number of artillery pieces, armored cars, and other military equipment, including&amp;nbsp;a number of aircraft.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;An international coalition, led by the United Kingdom, and including forces from Australia, New Zealand, and Singapore are&amp;nbsp;assisting Malaysia in its fight against the insurgents.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Complicating matters is that by 1973 the Soviet Union, the People's Republic of China, India,&amp;nbsp;North Korea, and Cuba have all&amp;nbsp; recognized the self-declared People's Republic of Kedah.&amp;nbsp; They have also made it clear they will not respect any attempt&amp;nbsp;by Malaysia or its allies to blockade any of the ports in the Kedah region, including the island of Langkawi.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;-------------------------------------------------------&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;A delta template .ini file has been included in the .zip file to assist in updating the scenario to any future versions of the database.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;Scenario Author: Mark Gellis&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
